      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under N2 using Schlenk techniques, a 150 mL Schlenk flask was charged with Cp2TiCl2 (0.75 g, 3.01 mmol), La powder (0.4 g, 2.9 mmol), HgCl2 (0.008 g, 0.029 mmol), ethanol (70 mL), and toluene (20 mL). The mixture was stirred under reflux for 35 h; the dark red solution changed to green then light yellow. The solution was filtered, concentrated under vacuum to 20 mL, layered with hexane (15 mL), and colorless crystals of 1 grew at room temperature after 8 weeks. Crystals were filtered, washed with hexane (3 × 5 mL), and dried under vacuum.",
